sys_script.script:
/**
 * SUPPRESSED -- the body below is intentionally commented out. The business rule record is kept
 * so the suppression is visible in the update set and reversible without recreating it.
 *
 * This is the label-mapping-table counterpart of the rule on the workload table (see
 * "Illumio Set Conflict"), suppressed for the same reason: IllumioDiscoveryUtils.evaluateConflict
 * now decides `conflicts` during discovery from values already in memory, and this rule ran
 * afterwards and re-decided it.
 *
 * Two specific problems it had on top of the redundancy:
 *
 *  - It only ever set `conflicts` to true, never back to false. A label row that came into
 *    agreement left the parent workload flagged as conflicting, so it kept being picked up by the
 *    sync chunk query on every subsequent run.
 *  - mappedField[current.illumio_pce_workload.source_table] is dereferenced with no guard. A
 *    workload whose source table has no class mapping yields undefined, and .indexOf on it throws
 *    inside a business rule on the label mapping table -- which is written to once per label per
 *    workload.
 *
 * If it is ever restored, both of those need fixing first.
 */

